<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b></b></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; color: #212529"><b></b></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b>Item 5.07 Submission of Matters to a Vote of
Security Holders.</b></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b>&#160;</b></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">On June 28, 2024, Dr. Steve Slilaty, as the holder
of the majority of the voting power of the stockholders of Sunshine Biopharma, Inc. (the &#8220;Company&#8221;), approved by written consent
an amendment to the Company&#8217;s articles of incorporation to effect a reverse split of the Company&#8217;s common stock at a ratio
of up to 60-for-1. The consent will be effective 20 days after the definitive information statement relating to such consent is mailed
to shareholders. As of June 28, 2024, Dr. Slilaty, who is the Company&#8217;s chief executive officer, held 84.8% of the total voting
power of the Company&#8217;s stockholders.</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b></b></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"></p>

